<title>UK: Waste Management marked up after ADR gains.</title>
<headline>Waste Management marked up after ADR gains.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Waste Management International Plc were up 11-1/2p to 250 by 0800 GMT as market makers adjusted prices after the group's American Depository Receipts (ADRs) rose in New York on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's just been priced in-line with the ADRs,&quot; one market maker said.</p>
<p>Waste Management ADRs rose $1/4 to $8 on Thursday, while shares in parent company WMX Technologies slipped $1/2 to $28-7/8.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
